            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The unregenerate human nature, the flesh, or spiritual impurity representing a heart not yielded to God that requires spiritual cleansing.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Deuteronomy 10:16\",\"Jeremiah 4:4\",\"Colossians 2:11\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Exclusion from God's covenant community and separation from the promises of Israel, often used as a marker for Gentiles.\",\"basis\":[\"Ephesians 2:11-12\",\"1 Samuel 17:26\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Spiritual deafness, stubbornness, and resistance to hearing God's word, often described as uncircumcised ears.\",\"basis\":[\"Jeremiah 6:10\",\"Acts 7:51\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"In Christian interpretation, physical uncircumcision transitions metaphorically in both the Prophets and the New Testament to denote spiritual alienation and rebellion, whereas spiritual circumcision represents regeneration and the cutting away of the sinful nature by Christ.\"}",
